luci-app-tr3600-fan: add a smart seasonal suggestion to the fan page

The fan page only offered two choices: the kernel's fixed step_wise curve,
or a manual level that has to be re-picked by hand whenever the weather
changes.  After 0007 the board is genuinely silent at its ~64 C idle, but
the right curve depends on the room: the same board that idles at 64 C in
October idles far higher in July, and nothing in the package knew the
difference.

Add a third mode, "smart", that picks the fan level from a seasonal curve,
and teach the LuCI page to show which curve fits and to switch in one click.

Curves (trip temperatures in millidegrees; the PWM steps are 0 / 50 % /
78 % / 100 %, i.e. the cooling-levels 0007 installed):

  winter   68000 78000 88000   identical to the DTS curve 0007 installs
  mild     66000 76000 86000   starts 2 C earlier
  summer   58000 68000 78000   starts 10 C earlier, actively cools down

The 5 C hysteresis matches the DTS (SEASON_HYST=5000), so a level is
released once the temperature drops 5 C below the trip that raised it.

The mild curve deliberately starts only 2 C below winter.  This board
measures 64.1 C with the fan stopped, so a first trip below that would
raise the fan and never release it again - the continuous low hum at idle
that 0006 and 0007 exist to eliminate.  Any future edit to these numbers
must keep every trip-1 above the measured fan-stopped idle temperature.

Season selection is deliberately NOT driven by the live temperature.  Load
pushes the temperature up, so a temperature-driven switch would flap
between seasons every time the router got busy.  The calendar picks the
season (Jun-Aug summer, Dec-Feb winter, otherwise mild); the measured
idle baseline - the lowest temperature seen while the fan was stopped,
which already carries the room temperature - is used by the LuCI page to
refine a *suggestion* that a human applies, not by the daemon.

The daemon keeps that baseline in /tmp/tr3600-fan.idle: it tracks the
lowest temperature seen with the fan at level 0, and drifts upwards by
10 mC per 10 s tick while the fan is running (3.6 C/h, capped at 95 C) so
a stale cold-weather value cannot survive a warm spell.  It lives in
/tmp, so it is re-learned after every boot.

Safety is unchanged: in smart mode the daemon still forces the fan to
level 3 at 100 C and hands control back to the kernel at 110 C.

Defaults are chosen so the out-of-box behaviour does not change: the
config still defaults to mode 'auto' (the kernel's step_wise curve), and
the new 'season' option defaults to 'auto' (calendar).  Smart mode is one
click away in the LuCI page.

Requires 0003: the view hunks use 0003's "dirty" flag lines as context.

Verified: sh -n on the helper, node --check on the view, and the seasonal
functions exercised against the measured fan-stopped idle (64.1 C stays at
level 0 under winter and mild, level 1 under summer) and across the
hysteresis boundaries.

Signed-off-by: TR3600 build kit <noreply@example.com>
